      "content": "hey so i'm just a temp helping out with this map digitization thing and i keep getting weird vibes from this one box of maps. like, there are these tiny little marks everywhere, they're not even like drawing marks, they're just these little clusters of scratches that look like they're scurrying into the corners or hiding under the borders. \n\nthey're so small and there's so many of them, it's almost like an infestation of ink or something. it's making me kinda jumpy lol. is there like a technical term for when a map looks like it's been... i don't know, nibbled on or cluttered with these tiny, random little things that don't belong there? i don't want to tell my boss it looks like pests did it but i dont know what else to call it.",
